Dear all,
When I estimate a model using MLR I get two columns, ML and MLR. For the first set of fit measures the indices vary as expected. However the three information criteria are always the same between the ML and robust columns (e.g. run summary(fitmlR, fit.measures=TRUE) below).

Nonetheless, estimating the same model using vanilla estimator='ml' will give a different BIC than when estimating using MLR. Shouldn't it be the case that the information indices in the ML column when estimating using estimator='mlr' should reflect the estimator='ml' BIC, rather than be identical to the MLR BIC? And if not, could you suggest why not?

HS.model <- ' visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3
              textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6
speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9 '

fitml <- cfa(HS.model, data=HolzingerSwineford1939)
summary(fitml, fit.measures=TRUE)
BIC(fitml)
fitmlR<-cfa(HS.model, data=HolzingerSwineford1939,estimator='mlr')
summary(fitmlR, fit.measures=TRUE)
BIC(fitmlR)

